.TH KBD-AUTOLIGHT 1 "October 2026" "kbd-autolight 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kbd-autolight \- automatic keyboard backlight from ambient light
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kbd-autolight
.RI { run " [" \-\-debug "] | " status " | " enable " | " disable " | " toggle " | " resume }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kbd-autolight
reads the ambient light sensor of the Lenovo Yoga Slim 7 ProX 14ARH7 and sets
the keyboard backlight through UPower: maximum level in the dark, low level in
dim light and off in a lit room. It runs as a systemd user service and pauses
itself for a while when the brightness is changed by hand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the service in the foreground. With
.BR \-\-debug ,
print every sensor reading.
.TP
.B status
Print the current state as JSON (used by the Plasma applet).
.TP
.B enable
Start the user service now and at every login.
.TP
.B disable
Stop the user service and keep it off.
.TP
.B toggle
Switch between enable and disable.
.TP
.B resume
Cancel a pause caused by a manual change.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kbd-autolight.conf
System-wide settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kbd-autolight.conf
Per-user settings; they override the system-wide file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR upower (1)
